    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d623">

                <pb facs="0753" n="679" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg679"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/2934</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Laughlin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-10-12T13:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 12, 1918, 1 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 9.56 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2737. Following from Stockholm: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>219, October 11, 1 p.m. Webster<anchor n="1" xml:id="d623-f1"/> arrived
                            yesterday with 7 Americans, 31 British, 29 French, including Lockhart, Ward,
                                Robin P. Lavergne and consular and military
                            staffs from Moscow. Forty-five British and 5 French still in fortress
                            Petrograd. Wardwell and
                                Andrews hope to come out shortly by boat.
                            Everything all right at Embassy. Rumor Kalamatiano shot in Moscow.
                            Seventeen more Americans arrive to-day. Whitehouse.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Archangel notified.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d623-f1" n="1" xml:id="d623-f1-content">
                <p>
                    Capt. William B. Webster, member of the
                    American Red Cross Commission to Russia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
